1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,526
The Bugatti Veyron has two secrets that

2
00:00:02,526 --> 00:00:04,017
most people never hear.

3
00:00:04,197 --> 00:00:06,838
First, at full speed it drinks fuel

4
00:00:06,838 --> 00:00:09,102
so fast that its tank is empty

5
00:00:09,102 --> 00:00:09,932
in minutes.

6
00:00:10,112 --> 00:00:12,285
Second, it can only reach its top

7
00:00:12,285 --> 00:00:13,932
speed with a special key,

8
00:00:13,932 --> 00:00:16,237
and the car checks itself before it

9
00:00:16,237 --> 00:00:17,554
will let you use it.

10
00:00:17,734 --> 00:00:20,449
Behind both sits a third surprise:

11
00:00:20,449 --> 00:00:23,245
the sources disagree on some of the

12
00:00:23,245 --> 00:00:24,363
basic numbers.

13
00:00:24,543 --> 00:00:25,940
Here is what we found,

14
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,527
with every claim sourced.

15
00:00:27,877 --> 00:00:30,657
The series today is about exotic cars,

16
00:00:30,657 --> 00:00:32,341
not only American ones,

17
00:00:32,341 --> 00:00:35,268
and Wikipedia says the Veyron belongs to

18
00:00:35,268 --> 00:00:36,805
the Volkswagen Group.

19
00:00:36,985 --> 00:00:38,673
We use Wikipedia,

20
00:00:38,673 --> 00:00:40,958
Top Gear, Car magazine,

21
00:00:40,958 --> 00:00:43,242
Motor One and Jalopnik.

22
00:00:43,422 --> 00:00:46,155
Where two sources give different numbers,

23
00:00:46,155 --> 00:00:47,021
we show both.

24
00:00:47,201 --> 00:00:49,342
Where we do the arithmetic,

25
00:00:49,342 --> 00:00:50,928
we label it as ours.

26
00:00:51,108 --> 00:00:53,077
And where a figure is a claim,

27
00:00:53,077 --> 00:00:54,324
we call it a claim.

28
00:00:54,675 --> 00:00:56,265
Start with the origin.

29
00:00:56,445 --> 00:01:00,298
Wikipedia says Volkswagen acquired the Bugatti name

30
00:01:00,298 --> 00:01:02,489
in May nineteen ninety-eight,

31
00:01:02,489 --> 00:01:05,814
the EB eighteen four Veyron concept appeared

32
00:01:05,814 --> 00:01:08,382
at the Tokyo Motor Show in October

33
00:01:08,382 --> 00:01:12,009
nineteen ninety-nine, and the production engine,

34
00:01:12,009 --> 00:01:12,915
a W sixteen,

35
00:01:12,915 --> 00:01:15,333
was shown in the EB sixteen four

36
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:16,542
in two thousand.

37
00:01:16,722 --> 00:01:19,695
Volkswagen Group decided to build the car

38
00:01:19,695 --> 00:01:21,145
in two thousand one.

39
00:01:21,496 --> 00:01:23,562
Motor One adds the pitch.

40
00:01:23,742 --> 00:01:25,726
In nineteen ninety-seven,

41
00:01:25,726 --> 00:01:27,710
it says, Ferdinand Piëch,

42
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:30,725
then chairman of the Volkswagen Group,

43
00:01:30,725 --> 00:01:34,216
pitched an eighteen-cylinder W engine car of

44
00:01:34,216 --> 00:01:37,946
one thousand metric horsepower and four hundred

45
00:01:37,946 --> 00:01:41,675
kilometres per hour to Volkswagen's engine head

46
00:01:41,675 --> 00:01:43,421
on a Shinkansen train.

47
00:01:43,601 --> 00:01:46,301
At the two thousand Geneva Motor Show,

48
00:01:46,301 --> 00:01:49,143
Piëch announced a target of one thousand

49
00:01:49,143 --> 00:01:51,914
one metric horsepower and four hundred.

50
00:01:52,263 --> 00:01:55,936
The first roadworthy prototype was finished in

51
00:01:55,936 --> 00:01:58,012
August two thousand three,

52
00:01:58,012 --> 00:02:01,924
Wikipedia says, and production began in September

53
00:02:01,924 --> 00:02:03,362
two thousand five,

54
00:02:03,362 --> 00:02:07,194
after technical problems caused repeated delays.

55
00:02:07,374 --> 00:02:08,661
By our arithmetic,

56
00:02:08,661 --> 00:02:11,235
that is five years and eleven months

57
00:02:11,235 --> 00:02:13,737
from the Tokyo concept to the first

58
00:02:13,737 --> 00:02:16,311
production cars, or about six years,

59
00:02:16,311 --> 00:02:19,027
and four years from the build decision

60
00:02:19,027 --> 00:02:20,958
to the start of production.

61
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:23,003
The name is a tribute.

62
00:02:23,183 --> 00:02:25,643
Wikipedia says the car is named after

63
00:02:25,643 --> 00:02:28,969
Pierre Veyron, who co-won the nineteen thirty-nine

64
00:02:28,969 --> 00:02:31,962
twenty-four Hours of Le Mans with Jean-Pierre

65
00:02:31,962 --> 00:02:32,494
Wimille.

66
00:02:32,674 --> 00:02:34,868
The EB stands for the founder,

67
00:02:34,868 --> 00:02:37,941
Ettore Bugatti, and sixteen four refers to

68
00:02:37,941 --> 00:02:40,940
sixteen cylinders and four turbochargers.

69
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,689
So the name carries a race winner,

70
00:02:43,689 --> 00:02:46,031
a founder and an engine layout.

71
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:47,367
Secret one.

72
00:02:47,547 --> 00:02:51,211
Wikipedia gives the Veyron's EPA fuel economy

73
00:02:51,211 --> 00:02:53,816
as eight miles per gallon in the

74
00:02:53,816 --> 00:02:56,258
city, fourteen on the highway,

75
00:02:56,258 --> 00:02:58,945
and three miles per gallon at top

76
00:02:58,945 --> 00:03:01,143
speed, or one point four U.

77
00:03:01,323 --> 00:03:01,717
S.

78
00:03:01,897 --> 00:03:03,047
gallons per minute.

79
00:03:03,227 --> 00:03:06,209
Take that last figure by our arithmetic:

80
00:03:06,209 --> 00:03:08,744
one point four gallons a minute is

81
00:03:08,744 --> 00:03:11,279
about eighty-four gallons an hour,

82
00:03:11,279 --> 00:03:13,814
which no road trip could ever use,

83
00:03:13,814 --> 00:03:16,647
because the car cannot keep that speed

84
00:03:16,647 --> 00:03:17,542
for an hour.

85
00:03:17,892 --> 00:03:20,434
Car magazine puts it more dramatically.

86
00:03:20,614 --> 00:03:22,906
It says that at full speed the

87
00:03:22,906 --> 00:03:25,732
car drains its one hundred litre fuel

88
00:03:25,732 --> 00:03:27,870
tank in just twelve minutes,

89
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:30,773
covering sixty-three and a half miles.

90
00:03:30,953 --> 00:03:32,810
The magazine's narrator,

91
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:36,755
Anthony ffrench-Constant, calls the car's top speed

92
00:03:36,755 --> 00:03:39,695
two hundred fifty-four miles per hour.

93
00:03:39,875 --> 00:03:41,211
So the fuel tank,

94
00:03:41,211 --> 00:03:42,469
in this telling,

95
00:03:42,469 --> 00:03:45,219
lasts about as long as a television

96
00:03:45,219 --> 00:03:46,005
programme.

97
00:03:46,356 --> 00:03:48,306
The two sources do not agree.

98
00:03:48,486 --> 00:03:51,605
Wikipedia's one point four gallons per minute

99
00:03:51,605 --> 00:03:53,962
is about five point three litres a

100
00:03:53,962 --> 00:03:56,874
minute, which over twelve minutes is about

101
00:03:56,874 --> 00:03:59,439
sixty-four litres, by our arithmetic,

102
00:03:59,439 --> 00:04:00,409
not a hundred.

103
00:04:00,589 --> 00:04:03,049
And a hundred litres in twelve minutes

104
00:04:03,049 --> 00:04:05,444
is eight point three litres a minute,

105
00:04:05,444 --> 00:04:07,451
or about two point two gallons.

106
00:04:07,631 --> 00:04:08,722
The tank size,

107
00:04:08,722 --> 00:04:11,683
the speed, or the rate differs between

108
00:04:11,683 --> 00:04:13,007
the two accounts,

109
00:04:13,007 --> 00:04:15,189
and neither source explains.

110
00:04:15,539 --> 00:04:18,335
There is a second inconsistency in Car's

111
00:04:18,335 --> 00:04:18,894
numbers.

112
00:04:19,074 --> 00:04:21,888
Sixty-three and a half miles in twelve

113
00:04:21,888 --> 00:04:25,147
minutes is three hundred seventeen miles per

114
00:04:25,147 --> 00:04:26,925
hour, by our arithmetic,

115
00:04:26,925 --> 00:04:29,813
which is faster than the car's maximum.

116
00:04:29,993 --> 00:04:33,225
At two hundred fifty-four miles per hour,

117
00:04:33,225 --> 00:04:36,379
twelve minutes covers about fifty miles.

118
00:04:36,559 --> 00:04:39,449
So the distance figure is also off.

119
00:04:39,629 --> 00:04:42,339
But the figure fits a different time:

120
00:04:42,339 --> 00:04:43,657
by our arithmetic,

121
00:04:43,657 --> 00:04:47,098
fifteen minutes at two hundred fifty-four miles

122
00:04:47,098 --> 00:04:49,807
per hour is exactly sixty-three and a

123
00:04:49,807 --> 00:04:50,612
half miles.

124
00:04:50,962 --> 00:04:54,144
The Wikipedia numbers do agree with themselves.

125
00:04:54,324 --> 00:04:56,944
Three miles per gallon at one point

126
00:04:56,944 --> 00:04:59,714
four gallons per minute is four point

127
00:04:59,714 --> 00:05:01,136
two miles a minute,

128
00:05:01,136 --> 00:05:02,484
by our arithmetic,

129
00:05:02,484 --> 00:05:05,478
which is two hundred fifty-two miles per

130
00:05:05,478 --> 00:05:05,852
hour.

131
00:05:06,032 --> 00:05:08,850
That matches the car's roughly two hundred

132
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:09,655
fifty-three.

133
00:05:09,835 --> 00:05:13,344
So the EPA-based figure is internally consistent,

134
00:05:13,344 --> 00:05:15,278
and we treat it as the more

135
00:05:15,278 --> 00:05:18,142
reliable pair, while noting that the Car

136
00:05:18,142 --> 00:05:21,007
magazine tank claim is only a magazine's

137
00:05:21,007 --> 00:05:21,723
statement.

138
00:05:22,074 --> 00:05:23,908
Even at normal speeds,

139
00:05:23,908 --> 00:05:25,742
the Veyron is thirsty.

140
00:05:25,922 --> 00:05:28,409
Eight miles per gallon in the city

141
00:05:28,409 --> 00:05:30,603
means that, by our arithmetic,

142
00:05:30,603 --> 00:05:33,601
ten thousand city miles would burn twelve

143
00:05:33,601 --> 00:05:35,210
hundred fifty gallons.

144
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:37,215
At fourteen on the highway,

145
00:05:37,215 --> 00:05:39,581
it would be seven hundred fourteen.

146
00:05:39,761 --> 00:05:41,574
We do not know the price of

147
00:05:41,574 --> 00:05:42,917
fuel where you live,

148
00:05:42,917 --> 00:05:44,394
so we stop at gallons.

149
00:05:44,574 --> 00:05:46,642
Multiply by the pump price and you

150
00:05:46,642 --> 00:05:47,616
have the number.

151
00:05:47,966 --> 00:05:49,452
Why so thirsty?

152
00:05:49,632 --> 00:05:51,292
The engine is large.

153
00:05:51,472 --> 00:05:54,530
Wikipedia lists the W sixteen at seven

154
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:58,796
thousand nine hundred ninety-three cubic centimetres,

155
00:05:58,796 --> 00:06:02,176
quad-turbocharged, with sixty-four valves.

156
00:06:02,356 --> 00:06:04,780
The base car makes one thousand one

157
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:08,450
metric horsepower, which is nine hundred eighty-seven

158
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:11,981
horsepower, and twelve hundred fifty newton-metres.

159
00:06:12,161 --> 00:06:15,032
The Super Sport makes twelve hundred metric

160
00:06:15,032 --> 00:06:19,039
horsepower, which is eleven hundred eighty-three horsepower,

161
00:06:19,039 --> 00:06:21,310
and fifteen hundred newton-metres.

162
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:24,326
Car magazine makes a good point about

163
00:06:24,326 --> 00:06:25,119
the engine.

164
00:06:25,299 --> 00:06:28,118
It says the W sixteen generates only

165
00:06:28,118 --> 00:06:31,876
some seventy-four brake horsepower per cylinder,

166
00:06:31,876 --> 00:06:34,616
about the same as a Volkswagen Golf

167
00:06:34,616 --> 00:06:34,773
R.

168
00:06:34,953 --> 00:06:36,325
By our arithmetic,

169
00:06:36,325 --> 00:06:40,060
eleven hundred eighty-three divided by sixteen is

170
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:41,965
seventy-three point nine,

171
00:06:41,965 --> 00:06:43,185
so that matches.

172
00:06:43,365 --> 00:06:46,035
The engine is not exotic per cylinder.

173
00:06:46,215 --> 00:06:48,199
It simply has sixteen of them,

174
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:49,721
and four turbochargers.

175
00:06:50,071 --> 00:06:52,009
All that power makes heat.

176
00:06:52,189 --> 00:06:55,607
Wikipedia says the Veyron has ten radiators:

177
00:06:55,607 --> 00:06:58,015
three for the intercooler loop,

178
00:06:58,015 --> 00:07:00,423
three for engine water cooling,

179
00:07:00,423 --> 00:07:03,375
and one each for the air conditioning,

180
00:07:03,375 --> 00:07:07,259
transmission oil, differential oil and engine oil.

181
00:07:07,439 --> 00:07:08,910
By our arithmetic,

182
00:07:08,910 --> 00:07:11,932
three plus three plus four singles is

183
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:14,219
ten, so the list checks out.

184
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:17,646
Car magazine says twelve radiators.

185
00:07:17,826 --> 00:07:19,765
Wikipedia says ten.

186
00:07:19,945 --> 00:07:22,660
We cannot tell whether the magazine is

187
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:26,660
counting differently, perhaps including heat exchangers,

188
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:28,803
or whether it is simply wrong.

189
00:07:28,983 --> 00:07:30,284
We show both.

190
00:07:30,464 --> 00:07:32,370
And the lesson is the same as

191
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:33,619
with the fuel tank:

192
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:35,065
for a car this famous,

193
00:07:35,065 --> 00:07:38,022
the basic numbers are repeated differently in

194
00:07:38,022 --> 00:07:40,914
different places, and you should check which

195
00:07:40,914 --> 00:07:42,689
source a figure comes from.

196
00:07:43,039 --> 00:07:45,526
Motor One tells the story behind the

197
00:07:45,526 --> 00:07:45,871
heat.

198
00:07:46,051 --> 00:07:47,770
Chief engineer Dr.

199
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:51,405
Wolfgang Schreiber recalled that above two hundred

200
00:07:51,405 --> 00:07:53,340
twenty-three miles per hour,

201
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,311
the driveshaft seals expanded and shredded,

202
00:07:56,311 --> 00:07:59,490
and the rear constant-velocity boots flung out

203
00:07:59,490 --> 00:08:00,941
their oil and failed.

204
00:08:01,121 --> 00:08:03,154
Motor One does not say how these

205
00:08:03,154 --> 00:08:04,488
problems were solved.

206
00:08:04,838 --> 00:08:08,056
Motor One says the engine changed from

207
00:08:08,056 --> 00:08:11,952
a naturally aspirated eighteen-cylinder W to a

208
00:08:11,952 --> 00:08:14,323
quad-turbocharged W sixteen.

209
00:08:14,503 --> 00:08:16,495
That was a major redesign,

210
00:08:16,495 --> 00:08:19,637
and it explains why production took until

211
00:08:19,637 --> 00:08:21,016
two thousand five.

212
00:08:21,196 --> 00:08:23,566
The goal, according to Motor One,

213
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:26,582
was one thousand one metric horsepower and

214
00:08:26,582 --> 00:08:28,952
four hundred kilometres per hour.

215
00:08:29,132 --> 00:08:30,418
By our arithmetic,

216
00:08:30,418 --> 00:08:33,206
four hundred kilometres per hour is two

217
00:08:33,206 --> 00:08:36,065
hundred forty-eight and a half miles per

218
00:08:36,065 --> 00:08:36,423
hour.

219
00:08:36,773 --> 00:08:38,793
Secret two is the key.

220
00:08:38,973 --> 00:08:41,922
Top Gear says that the Veyron's normal

221
00:08:41,922 --> 00:08:45,103
top speed is two hundred thirty-six miles

222
00:08:45,103 --> 00:08:48,130
per hour, and that reaching two hundred

223
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:51,622
fifty-three requires inserting a special key,

224
00:08:51,622 --> 00:08:52,553
a Speed Key,

225
00:08:52,553 --> 00:08:55,424
into a slot beside the driver's seat.

226
00:08:55,604 --> 00:08:58,028
Turning the key starts a series of

227
00:08:58,028 --> 00:08:59,168
computer checks.

228
00:08:59,348 --> 00:09:01,854
The car grants access to Top Speed

229
00:09:01,854 --> 00:09:04,875
mode only if specific conditions are met.

230
00:09:05,225 --> 00:09:07,988
Wikipedia gives a different normal figure.

231
00:09:08,168 --> 00:09:10,755
It says the normally listed top speed

232
00:09:10,755 --> 00:09:14,181
is three hundred forty-three kilometres per hour,

233
00:09:14,181 --> 00:09:16,908
or two hundred thirteen miles per hour,

234
00:09:16,908 --> 00:09:19,426
and that the full top speed requires

235
00:09:19,426 --> 00:09:20,405
a special key.

236
00:09:20,585 --> 00:09:23,254
So two sources agree about the key

237
00:09:23,254 --> 00:09:25,765
and disagree about the baseline:

238
00:09:25,765 --> 00:09:29,455
two hundred thirteen or two hundred thirty-six.

239
00:09:29,635 --> 00:09:30,921
By our arithmetic,

240
00:09:30,921 --> 00:09:33,493
that is a twenty-three mile per hour

241
00:09:33,493 --> 00:09:34,279
difference.

242
00:09:34,629 --> 00:09:37,415
Car magazine describes a middle step.

243
00:09:37,595 --> 00:09:40,333
At one hundred twelve miles per hour,

244
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:43,440
it says, the car switches automatically to

245
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:46,622
handling mode, lowering the ride height and

246
00:09:46,622 --> 00:09:48,397
deploying the rear wing,

247
00:09:48,397 --> 00:09:52,171
with downforce of one hundred twenty-five kilograms

248
00:09:52,171 --> 00:09:54,538
at the front and four hundred at

249
00:09:54,538 --> 00:09:57,720
the rear, good for two hundred thirty-three

250
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,830
miles per hour.

251
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,116
To go faster,

252
00:10:00,116 --> 00:10:03,267
the driver pulls over and inserts the

253
00:10:03,267 --> 00:10:04,118
speed key.

254
00:10:04,468 --> 00:10:06,325
What the key does is physical.

255
00:10:06,505 --> 00:10:08,921
Top Gear says front ride height drops

256
00:10:08,921 --> 00:10:12,511
from one hundred twenty-five millimetres to sixty-five,

257
00:10:12,511 --> 00:10:14,470
and the rear drops to seventy.

258
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:17,229
The rear wing lowers and angles to

259
00:10:17,229 --> 00:10:20,339
two degrees, and the diffuser flaps close

260
00:10:20,339 --> 00:10:21,476
to reduce drag.

261
00:10:21,656 --> 00:10:24,243
Car magazine says it takes all but

262
00:10:24,243 --> 00:10:26,602
three degrees of rear wing off.

263
00:10:26,782 --> 00:10:28,179
By our arithmetic,

264
00:10:28,179 --> 00:10:30,663
the front of the car drops sixty

265
00:10:30,663 --> 00:10:33,922
millimetres, nearly two and a half inches.

266
00:10:34,273 --> 00:10:35,538
And the car can say no.

267
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:39,892
Top Gear says slightly incorrect tyre pressure,

268
00:10:39,892 --> 00:10:43,355
for example, blocks access to Top Speed

269
00:10:43,355 --> 00:10:43,799
mode.

270
00:10:43,979 --> 00:10:46,431
So the Veyron's top speed is not

271
00:10:46,431 --> 00:10:48,193
only a matter of power.

272
00:10:48,373 --> 00:10:50,161
It is a check list that the

273
00:10:50,161 --> 00:10:52,411
car runs before it lets the driver

274
00:10:52,411 --> 00:10:53,934
do something dangerous.

275
00:10:54,114 --> 00:10:56,165
That is an unusual idea for a

276
00:10:56,165 --> 00:10:58,004
road car, and it is why we

277
00:10:58,004 --> 00:10:59,559
call the key a secret.

278
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:02,023
The rear wing has another job.

279
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:05,153
Car magazine says that at fifty-five degrees

